---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const perspectives = [
    {
        title: "Coaching",
        body: "ICF-accredited coaching that helps you explore your assumptions, values, motivations and the questions you might be avoiding."
    },
    {
        title: "Gestalt",
        body: "I'm currently in my second year of a four-year Gestalt training programme. It brings an additional perspective on awareness, relationships, patterns and how we experience ourselves in the world."
    },
    {
        title: "Career strategy",
        body: "Practical thinking about the job market, professional positioning, transferable skills, leadership and the different ways your experience can translate into what's next."
    }
];

const credentials = [
    "8+ years of experience in international tech, including leadership roles at Preply and Qonto",
    "90+ coaching processes and 350+ hours of coaching experience",
    "Experience hiring and building teams across multiple professional disciplines",
    "Gestalt training, currently in year two of a four-year programme",
    "Based in Paris, working with people internationally"
];

const quotes = [
    {
        text: "Kate's approach helped me see myself and my potential in a new light.",
        author: "Yana A."
    },
    {
        text: "She guided me to understand what will work best for me — not just following external signals and trends.",
        author: "Marta R."
    },
    {
        text: "Kate helped me dig out a much bigger problem — and move forward with a truly pivotal decision for me and my family.",
        author: "Anonymous"
    }
];
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Kate Mas — Career Strategist & Coach | Paris"
    description="Kate Mas is an ICF ACC career coach and former tech leader helping experienced professionals make sense of where they are and decide what's next. Based in Paris, working internationally."
>
    <!-- 1 — BEIGE: Intro -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24 bg-background">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6">
            <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_16rem] lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_20rem] gap-10 md:gap-12 lg:gap-14 items-center">
                <div>
                    <p class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-4">
                        About Kate Mas
                    </p>
                    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-foreground leading-tight mb-6 sm:mb-8">
                        Career paths are rarely as straightforward as they look on LinkedIn.
                    </h1>
                    <div class="space-y-5 font-sans text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
                        <p class="text-foreground">
                            I'm Kate. Career coach, former tech leader, and
                            someone who's changed countries, industries,
                            professional identities and plans more than once.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            I've spent most of my career figuring things out as
                            I go. Sometimes by choice, sometimes because life
                            had other plans.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            I've gone from studying communications and media to
                            building content teams in startups and leading UX
                            writing in fintech, and eventually from a
                            comfortable leadership career to building my own
                            coaching practice.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="max-w-xs mx-auto md:max-w-none w-full photo-frame photo-tilt-right">
                    <img src="/about/kate-rug.jpg" alt="Kate Mas sitting cross-legged on a rug in a yellow striped shirt" width="724" height="1086" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2 — BLUE: Who I work with -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24 bg-primary text-primary-foreground">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6">
            <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
                <p class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-6">
                    Who I work with
                </p>
                <p class="font-sans font-medium text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-snug mb-8">
                    Today, I work with experienced professionals who find
                    themselves somewhere in between: they've built successful
                    careers, developed expertise and earned their place at the
                    table. But something isn't quite working anymore.
                </p>
                <div class="space-y-5 font-sans text-base sm:text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/70 mb-10">
                    <p>
                        Maybe you've outgrown your role. Maybe the career you've
                        worked so hard to build no longer reflects who you are.
                        Or maybe you're looking at the next 10 years and
                        wondering whether you actually want more of the same.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        I know that feeling. And I don't think the answer is
                        always to quit, start over or follow your passion.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <blockquote class="font-accent text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-snug text-secondary border-l-2 border-secondary pl-5 sm:pl-6">
                    Sometimes the most interesting work is figuring out what
                    you want to keep, what needs to change, and what you
                    haven't considered yet.
                </blockquote>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3 — BEIGE: Both sides -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24 bg-background">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6">
            <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
                <p class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-4">
                    My background
                </p>
                <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl text-foreground leading-tight mb-8 sm:mb-10">
                    I've been on both sides of the career conversation.
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-5 font-sans text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
                    <p>
                        Before becoming a full-time career coach, I spent over
                        eight years working in tech, across edtech and fintech.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        I joined <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Preply</span>
                        when it was a team of around 40 people. Over five years,
                        I helped build its copywriting function from the ground
                        up, eventually leading a team and contributing to the
                        company's growth through multiple funding rounds.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Then came <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Qonto</span>,
                        where I moved to Paris and took on a leadership role in
                        one of France's leading fintech companies. I managed UX
                        writers, worked on content systems and helped build the
                        foundations for consistent product communication across
                        multiple markets.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Along the way, I've hired and worked with senior
                        professionals across different disciplines, from
                        designers and content specialists to localization
                        professionals.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        I've seen how companies grow, how teams change, how
                        leadership expectations evolve and how careers can look
                        very different from the inside than they do on paper.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="mt-10 sm:mt-12 bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-foreground mb-4">
                        That experience matters in my coaching.
                    </h3>
                    <p class="font-sans text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground mb-6">
                        I understand that career decisions don't happen in a
                        vacuum. There's a mortgage, a salary, a professional
                        reputation, a family, a visa, a team that depends on
                        you — and sometimes a very real fear of losing
                        everything you've worked for.
                    </p>
                    <p class="font-accent text-xl sm:text-2xl leading-snug text-primary">
                        I won't tell you to quit your job and figure it out
                        later. That's not a career strategy.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 4 — BLUE: From building teams to coaching -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24 bg-primary text-primary-foreground">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6">
            <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
                <p class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-4">
                    How I got here
                </p>
                <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-tight mb-8 sm:mb-10">
                    From building teams to helping people rebuild their careers.
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-5 font-sans text-base sm:text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/70">
                    <p>
                        I've always been interested in people: what drives them,
                        how they make decisions, what gets in their way and what
                        makes work meaningful.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Coaching was initially something I wanted to explore
                        alongside my leadership career. Eventually, it became
                        the work I wanted to dedicate myself to.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Since 2024, I've been working with professionals
                        navigating career transitions, leadership challenges,
                        professional identity questions and the occasional
                        existential career crisis.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-primary-foreground">
                        Today, my work combines three perspectives:
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 sm:gap-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto mt-8 sm:mt-10">
                {
                    perspectives.map((item, i) => (
                        <div class="bg-primary-foreground/10 border border-primary-foreground/20 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl">
                            <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-secondary flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
                                <span class="font-serif text-xl text-primary">{i + 1}</span>
                            </div>
                            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">{item.title}</h3>
                            <p class="font-sans text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/70">
                                {item.body}
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    ))
                }
            </div>

            <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-10 sm:mt-12 space-y-4">
                <p class="font-sans text-base sm:text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/70">
                    I'm not here to hand you a five-step formula or tell you
                    what your next job should be.
                </p>
                <p class="font-accent text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-snug text-secondary">
                    I'm here to help you make sense of where you are, explore
                    what's possible and make decisions that actually belong to
                    you.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 5 — BEIGE: Credentials -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24 bg-background">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6">
            <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
                <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl text-foreground text-center mb-10 sm:mb-14">
                    A little more about my work
                </h2>
                <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 sm:gap-5">
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://www.credly.com/badges/a7c85c18-7eba-4f5e-b557-d5ea999503c3/public_url"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            class="group h-full flex items-start gap-4 bg-secondary/60 hover:bg-secondary transition-colors border border-primary/10 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6"
                        >
                            <span class="text-2xl leading-none" aria-hidden="true">🏅</span>
                            <span class="font-sans text-base text-foreground leading-snug flex-1">
                                ICF ACC credentialed coach
                                <span class="mt-2 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">
                                    View badge
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2V8a2 2 0 012-2h6M15 3h6v6M10 14L21 3" /></svg>
                                </span>
                            </span>
                        </a>
                    </li>
                    {
                        credentials.map((item) => (
                            <li class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6">
                                <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-primary" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7" /></svg>
                                <span class="font-sans text-base text-foreground leading-snug">{item}</span>
                            </li>
                        ))
                    }
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 6 — BLUE: What working with me feels like -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24 bg-primary text-primary-foreground">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6">
            <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid md:grid-cols-[18rem_1fr] gap-10 md:gap-14 items-start">
                <div class="max-w-xs w-full mx-auto md:max-w-none md:sticky md:top-28 photo-frame photo-frame-sky photo-tilt-left">
                    <img src="/about/kate-thoughtful.jpg" alt="Kate Mas sitting on a chair, looking to the side" width="724" height="1086" loading="lazy" />
                </div>
                <div>
                <p class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-4">
                    My approach
                </p>
                <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-tight mb-8 sm:mb-10">
                    What working with me feels like
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-5 font-sans text-base sm:text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/70">
                    <p>
                        I'll listen carefully, ask questions and challenge you
                        when I think you're overlooking something.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        I'm not particularly interested in helping you create a
                        more impressive version of your LinkedIn profile if you
                        haven't figured out what you want it to communicate.
                    </p>
                    <p class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-primary-foreground">
                        I believe clarity should come before action.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        That means we might spend time understanding why you're
                        dissatisfied before discussing your next move. We might
                        question whether you actually want a promotion, whether
                        management is still right for you, or whether the
                        industry you've built your identity around is still
                        where you want to be.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Sometimes the answer is a new job. Sometimes it's a
                        different way of working in the same company. Sometimes
                        it's a completely different direction.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        And sometimes, the biggest change is how you see
                        yourself and the experience you've already accumulated.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <blockquote class="mt-10 font-accent text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-snug text-secondary border-l-2 border-secondary pl-5 sm:pl-6">
                    The goal isn't to make your career look good from the
                    outside. It's to make it work better for you.
                </blockquote>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 7 — BEIGE: Client quotes -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24 bg-background">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6">
            <div class="text-center mb-10 sm:mb-14">
                <p class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-4">
                    Client stories
                </p>
                <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl text-foreground max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-tight">
                    A few things people I've worked with have said
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 sm:gap-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
                {
                    quotes.map((q) => (
                        <figure class="bg-card p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border flex flex-col">
                            <blockquote class="font-accent text-base sm:text-lg text-foreground leading-snug flex-grow mb-5">
                                "{q.text}"
                            </blockquote>
                            <figcaption class="font-sans text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                                — {q.author}
                            </figcaption>
                        </figure>
                    ))
                }
            </div>
            <div class="text-center mt-8 sm:mt-10">
                <a href="/reviews" class="link-arrow">
                    Read more client stories
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 8 — BLUE: Outside of work -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24 bg-primary text-primary-foreground">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6">
            <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid md:grid-cols-[18rem_1fr] gap-10 md:gap-14 items-center">
                <div class="max-w-xs w-full mx-auto md:max-w-none photo-frame photo-frame-sky photo-tilt-right">
                    <img src="/about/kate-kick.jpg" alt="Kate Mas mid-kick, leaning back and laughing" width="724" height="1086" loading="lazy" />
                </div>
                <div>
                <p class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-4">
                    Off the clock
                </p>
                <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-tight mb-8 sm:mb-10">
                    Outside of work
                </h2>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8">
                    <span class="font-sans text-xs font-bold bg-secondary text-primary px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider">🇺🇦 Ukraine</span>
                    <span class="font-sans text-xs font-bold bg-secondary text-primary px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider">🇨🇾 Cyprus</span>
                    <span class="font-sans text-xs font-bold bg-secondary text-primary px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider">🇮🇹 Italy</span>
                    <span class="font-sans text-xs font-bold bg-secondary text-primary px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider">🇫🇷 France</span>
                </div>
                <div class="space-y-5 font-sans text-base sm:text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/70">
                    <p>
                        I've lived in four countries: Ukraine, Cyprus, Italy and
                        France. I speak five languages, although my French still
                        gives me plenty of opportunities to practise humility.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        I've studied communications and media, worked night shifts to
                        support myself through university, built a career in
                        startups and relocated internationally more than once.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        I'm a curious person by nature. I like learning,
                        questioning things and occasionally getting myself into
                        situations where I have absolutely no idea what I'm
                        doing.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Currently, that includes Gestalt training, tennis, the
                        art of bonsai and figuring out how to build a sustainable business that gives me the
                        same freedom I want my clients to find in their own
                        careers.
                    </p>
                </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 9 — BEIGE: CTA -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24 bg-background">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6">
            <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_18rem] gap-10 md:gap-14 items-center text-center md:text-left">
            <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl text-foreground mb-6 sm:mb-8">
                So, where are you in your career?
            </h2>
            <div class="max-w-xl mx-auto md:mx-0 space-y-4 font-sans text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground mb-8 sm:mb-10">
                <p>
                    If you're in that uncomfortable space between what you've
                    built and what you want next, we should talk.
                </p>
                <p>
                    You don't need to have a clear plan. You don't even need to
                    know whether you want to stay or leave.
                </p>
                <p class="text-foreground">
                    That's what we can figure out together.
                </p>
            </div>
            <a href="/intro-call" class="btn-primary btn-lg">Let's talk</a>
            </div>
            <div class="max-w-xs w-full mx-auto md:max-w-none photo-frame photo-tilt-left">
                <img src="/about/kate-smiling.jpg" alt="Kate Mas smiling, hand on hip, in a yellow striped shirt" width="724" height="1086" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
